memory representation :
4GB memory => 4G x 1B == (no of cells is 4G)x(capacity of each cell is 1byte).

calculate how many bits adds is required for 4GB memory
No of cells => 4G == (2^2)x(2^30) == 2^32
formula of adds size => if no of cells 2^x then x is the adds size,so
adds size => 32 bits for 4GB memory

note :
1)byte addrsable memory means on each adds location we can store 1 byte data
2)word addrsable memory means on each adds location we can strore 1 word

